 steps** — how to verify a successful air-gapped install (e.g.,\n  confirming InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode).\n- **Troubleshooting** — the three most common field-reported failure modes:\n  image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n\nThe guide covers raw deployment mode only; serverless-mode disconnected support\nis out of scope, as is any change to code, operators, or default configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in\n   the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration,\n   and validation steps.\n2. The guide's image-mirroring reference lists the required images for a\n   disconnected KServe raw deployment install and documents how to derive the\n   digest list for a given release.\n3. The guide's troubleshooting section covers image pull errors, missing\n   runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n4. Every technical claim about KServe raw deployment mode in the guide is\n   validated against the KServe architecture context — specifically that raw\n   deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no Service Mesh /\n   Serverless dependency and is the recommended path for disconnected\n   environments — and any discrepancy found during authoring is resolved before\n   publication.\n5. The guide is technically reviewed and signed off by the serving team before\n   publication, confirming the documented steps match actual disconnected\n   cluster behavior.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n  covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps —\n  delivered by this epic's guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, and\n  validation sections).\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Complete image-mirroring reference with required images and\n  per-release digest derivation — delivered by this epic's image-mirroring\n  reference section.\n- **HLR-3 (P2)**: Troubleshooting section covering the three most common\n  field-reported failure modes — delivered by this epic's troubleshooting\n  section.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23028,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96faffa2b1418b2f","agent_id":"a57d4b02009a9d58f","session_id":"ebc27a66-d40e-4554-89a1-445e8c48ce5b","uuid":"d26a5420-8a53-4f69-82c0-aee694ac7575","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:05:54.903Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9004"}
