{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2641c106e7ab06f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a disconnected-environment (air-gapped) install guide for\n34\tKServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. Raw deployment mode —\n35\tplain Deployments and Services with no Service Mesh / Serverless dependency —\n36\tis the recommended KServe path for disconnected clusters, but the current\n37\tdocumentation only covers serverless-mode installs, leaving field teams to\n38\trediscover the mirroring, operator, and validation steps in private gists.\n39\tSource material already exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring\n40\tand technical review work only. No product behavior, code, operator, or default\n41\tconfiguration changes are in scope — the capability exists and works today.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\tAuthor and technically review a new documentation topic covering a disconnected\n46\tinstall of KServe in raw deployment mode. Content outline:\n47\t\n48\t- **Prerequisites** — requirements for a disconnected cluster running KServe in\n49\t  raw deployment mode (e.g., access to a mirrored container registry, tooling\n50\t  needed before starting, supported install path).\n51\t- **Operator configuration** — which operators are required for raw deployment\n52\t  mode and which are not needed because raw mode has no mesh dependency\n53\t  (Service Mesh / Serverless operators are serverless-mode only).\n54\t- **Image-mirroring reference** — the complete list of images required for a\n55\t  disconnected KServe raw deployment install, plus the method for deriving the\n56\t  per-release digest list so the reference stays accurate across releases.\n57\t- **Validation steps** — how to verify a successful air-gapped install (e.g.,\n58\t  confirming InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode).\n59\t- **Troubleshooting** — the three most common field-reported failure modes:\n60\t  image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n61\t\n62\tThe guide covers raw deployment mode only; serverless-mode disconnected support\n63\tis out of scope, as is any change to code, operators, or default configuration.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t1. A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in\n68\t   the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration,\n69\t   and validation steps.\n70\t2. The guide's image-mirroring reference lists the required images for a\n71\t   disconnected KServe raw deployment install and documents how to derive the\n72\t   digest list for a given release.\n73\t3. The guide's troubleshooting section covers image pull errors, missing\n74\t   runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n75\t4. Every technical claim about KServe raw deployment mode in the guide is\n76\t   validated against the KServe architecture context — specifically that raw\n77\t   deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no Service Mesh /\n78\t   Serverless dependency and is the recommended path for disconnected\n79\t   environments — and any discrepancy found during authoring is resolved before\n80\t   publication.\n81\t5. The guide is technically reviewed and signed off by the serving team before\n82\t   publication, confirming the documented steps match actual disconnected\n83\t   cluster behavior.\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n88\t  covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps —\n89\t  delivered by this epic's guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, and\n90\t  validation sections).\n91\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Complete image-mirroring reference with required images and\n92\t  per-release digest derivation — delivered by this epic's image-mirroring\n93\t  reference section.\n94\t- **HLR-3 (P2)**: Troubleshooting section covering the three most common\n95\t  field-reported failure modes — delivered by this epic's troubleshooting\n96\t  section.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad6b846a2fc95bb0","agent_id":"abc1a654ac50ce1e1","session_id":"ebc27a66-d40e-4554-89a1-445e8c48ce5b","uuid":"2a5d28ab-ef5f-4494-ae5f-4b404764db57","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:07:27.725Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2641c106e7ab06f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
